<title>UK: Commerzbank Overseas sets $75 mln four-year bond.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank Overseas sets $75 mln four-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following step-up bond was announced by joint lead managers Kredietbank and Commerzbank.</p>
<p> BORROWER   COMMERZBANK OVERSEAS FINANCE NV</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  COMMERZBANK AG</p>
<p> AMT    $75 MLN	 COUPON     *5.0	MATURITY    23.JAN.01</p>
<p> TYPE	 STEP-UP   ISS PRICE  101.771   PAY DATE  L-22.JAN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.625     REOFFER    100.371   SPREAD	+6 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA2	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA-	 DENOMS (K) 1-5	 SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.225     SELL CONC  1.40	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND INTERPOLATED NOVEMBER 1999 AND SEPTEMBER</p>
<p>			     2001 TREASURIES</p>
<p> NOTES	*FOR YEARS ONE AND TWO, 7.50 PCT THEREAFTER</p>
<p>		L-LONG FIRST COUPON</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
